   "longComment": "Patterson's only field goal was a 29-yard chip shot late in the third quarter, but he missed his first point-after try of the season late in the fourth quarter. He's attempted only one field goal in each of the Dolphins' last three games, and his weekly scoring floor figures to be lower than most kickers given that Miami averages only 14.0 points per game this season, which is second-worst in the NFL only behind the Titans (11.6). The Dolphins are on a bye Week 6 before hitting the road for a Week 7 AFC East tilt against the Jets on Sunday, Oct. 25.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642125",
   "name": "Kevin Coleman Jr.",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-12T02:15Z",
   "shortComment": "Coleman caught three of seven targets for 30 yards and a touchdown during Sunday's 31-24 loss to the Bengals.",
   "longComment": "Coleman finished second on the team in targets behind fellow wide receiver Malik Washington (eight). Coleman's most significant moment in Week 5 came in the fourth quarter when he reeled in a three-yard touchdown pass from quarterback Malik Willis. Coleman has now caught five of 17 targets for 36 yards and a touchdown over five contests this season.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642063",
   "name": "Malik Washington",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T23:54Z",
   "shortComment": "Washington secured six of eight targets for 43 yards, rushed once for 18 yards, returned two kickoffs for 45 yards and ran back one punt for 28 yards in the Dolphins' 31-24 loss to the Bengals on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Washington led the Dolphins across the board in receptions, receiving yards and targets during Caleb Douglas' third straight absence because of an ankle injury, although the middle total was relatively modest on an afternoon in which Malik Willis threw for just 137 yards. Washington's catch total was also a new season high, and he's now upped his reception tally over that of the previous week in four consecutive contests. Washington will remain a relevant asset in deeper PPR formats and as a DFS dart throw in a Week 7 road matchup against the Jets on Sunday, Oct. 25, following a Week 6 bye.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642060",
   "name": "Malik Willis",
   "pos": "QB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T23:47Z",
   "shortComment": "Willis completed 15 of 27 passes for 137 yards with one touchdown and two interceptions and added eight carries for 74 yards and another score in the Dolphins' 31-24 loss to the Bengals on Sunday. He also committed two fumbles, losing one and recovering the other.",
   "longComment": "Willis had a particularly difficult first half through the air, and although he was able to bring up his numbers somewhat in the second half, he still finished with his second-fewest passing yards of the season. Willis connected with Kevin Coleman for a three-yard touchdown just past the midway point of the fourth quarter, but the veteran signal-caller made more of an impact on the ground with a season-high rushing yardage total and his second rushing touchdown of the campaign . Willis is helping keep the Dolphins competitive most weeks, so he figures to remain under center for a Week 7 divisional road matchup against the Jets on Sunday, Oct. 25, following a Week 6 bye.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642042",
   "name": "Ollie Gordon II",
   "pos": "RB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T23:06Z",
   "shortComment": "Gordon rushed 18 times for 88 yards and a touchdown in the Dolphins' 31-24 loss to the Bengals on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Gordon turned in a useful fantasy performance in the lead role once again, even as he navigated a brief exit from the game due to an undisclosed injury in the second half. The second-year back was able to still handle a robust workload despite the Dolphins trailing for the majority of the game, and he finished with a new career high in rush attempts. Gordon also recorded a rushing touchdown for the third straight game when he went in from one yard with just over eight minutes remaining in the first quarter, and he should continue to helm Miami's ground attack in a Week 7 road matchup against the Jets on Sunday, Oct. 25, following a Week 6 bye.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641987",
   "name": "JuJu Brents",
   "pos": "CB",
   "status": "Questionable",
   "date": "2026-10-11T19:53Z",
   "shortComment": "Brents exited in the fourth quarter of Sunday's game against the Bengals due to a stinger and is questionable to return.",
   "longComment": "Brents had initially been labeled as questionable to return after leaving the game in the first half to receive evaluation for a concussion as well as the stinger. He was able to check back into the game to begin the second half, but he appears to have suffered an aggravation of the stinger. Brents tallied six tackles and one pass breakup prior to his most recent exit.",
